# Environment variables file  
.env 
# User-supplied model weights and whisper.cpp binaries.
# Ignored wholesale rather than file-by-file: a single ggml model is ~250 MB,
# well past GitHub's 100 MB per-file push limit, and listing binaries
# individually meant any newly added .dll slipped through. Both folders are
# documented in README.md / SETUP_AMD.md as things you download yourself.
# _models/* rather than _models/ : git does not descend into an ignored
# DIRECTORY, so a negation for anything inside one can never match. Ignoring
# the contents instead is what lets the small Silero export below be kept.
_models/*
!_models/silero_vad*.onnx
_whisper.cpp/
_whisper.cpp.bck/

# Saved transcripts (--save; auto-named transcript_YYYYmmdd_HHMMSS.txt)
transcript_*.txt
my_transcript.txt

# Saved presets are personal setups; the folder is kept, its contents are not.
presets/*.json

# ============================================================
#  Desktop panel (ui/) - .NET
#
#  ui/runtime IS committed, deliberately. It is 6.4 MB of publish output and
#  it is what lets a fresh clone run the panel with only the .NET Desktop
#  runtime - no SDK, no NuGet restore, no network. The alternative is a fetch
#  script that costs every cloner the SDK. Re-run build_ui.cmd and commit the
#  result after changing anything under ui/.
#
#  Everything else .NET produces is per-machine and must stay out.
# ============================================================
ui/bin/
ui/obj/
ui/**/bin/
ui/**/obj/

# Debug symbols: per-build, and of no use to someone running the panel.
ui/runtime/*.pdb

# Visual Studio / Rider per-user state.
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.userprefs

# Default output of ui/tools/shot.py when no path is given.
/panel.png
